<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Federation of Rhodesia and Nyasaland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1953">1953</a>–<a href="/years/1963">1963</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Central African Federation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Federation of Rhodesia and Nyasaland, or Central African Federation, joined the British territories of Southern Rhodesia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-rhodesia">Northern Rhodesia</a> and Nyasaland from 1953 to 1963. Dominated by white settlers and governed from Salisbury, it faced strong African opposition. It was dissolved in 1963, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malawi">Malawi</a> became independent and Southern Rhodesia declared independence as Rhodesia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/federation-of-rhodesia-and-nyasaland.jpg" alt="Federation of Rhodesia and Nyasaland" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown , vector version by Lupin, Greentubing, Fenn-O-maniC and NikNaks · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Rhodesia_and_Nyasaland_(1953%E2%80%931963).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
